# The same brief as 07-crushline, answered without touching the grid.
#
# Four turbines drive two crushers, a mill and a separator directly. No
# generator, no motor, no electricity anywhere in the machine: rotary is a
# domain, and a turbine already makes it, so putting it through a generator and
# back through a motor would be two conversions and 19% for nothing.
#
# What it costs is everything the power brief was trying to minimise -- a
# reactor, four exchangers, three pumps, 350 water a tick and a long heat main
# across the plant to the pair of exchangers that could not fit beside the
# reactor. Twenty components against fifteen, on twice the plot, for roughly the
# same ore. That is the trade, stated in numbers, and neither answer is wrong.
#
# This is also the design the note that started experiment 07 asked for: several
# machines hanging off one drive, which nothing anywhere had to be told was
# allowed -- and which, as it turns out, never needed a line shaft to say so.
# T3 and T4 both feed the mill and both feed the separator, four wires, and the
# ports divide what arrives.

machine "Steam Crusher"
brief crush

inlet     I1  at 0,0   draws ore
crusher   C1  at 4,0
crusher   C2  at 9,0
mill      MI1 at 14,0
separator S1  at 19,0
outlet    O1  at 24,0
skip      SK1 at 24,3

gearbox   GB1 at 5,7   ratio 4

turbine   T1  at 0,5
turbine   T2  at 11,5
turbine   T3  at 18,5
turbine   T4  at 18,8

exchanger HX1 at 0,8
exchanger HX2 at 11,8
exchanger HX3 at 23,5
exchanger HX4 at 23,9

reactor   R1  at 10,12
pump      W1  at 0,12
pump      W2  at 16,12
pump      W3  at 28,7

wire I1.out -> C1.in
wire C1.out -> C2.in
wire C2.out -> MI1.in
wire MI1.out -> S1.in
wire S1.rich -> O1.solid
wire S1.tails -> SK1.solid

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX3.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX4.heat

wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W2.water -> HX2.water
wire W3.water -> HX3.water
wire W3.water -> HX4.water

wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T2.steam
wire HX3.steam -> T3.steam
wire HX4.steam -> T4.steam

wire T1.rotary -> GB1.in
wire T2.rotary -> GB1.in
wire GB1.out -> C1.drive
wire GB1.out -> C2.drive

wire T3.rotary -> MI1.drive
wire T4.rotary -> MI1.drive
wire T3.rotary -> S1.drive
wire T4.rotary -> S1.drive
